FINDING 1 (low confidence): s02:net/ipv6/exthdrs.c:137-141, quote 'while (len > 0) {
		int optlen = nh[off + 1] + 2;
		int i;

		switch (nh[off]) {'. ip6_parse_tlv() (called from ipv6_parse_hopopts exthdrs.c:1039 and ipv6_destopt_rcv exthdrs.c:308 on remotely received IPv6 hop-by-hop/destination option headers) executes 'int optlen = nh[off + 1] + 2' at line 138 BEFORE the type-byte switch and before any len>=2 check; the only remaining-length guard 'if (optlen > len) goto bad' sits in the default case after the length byte was read. With len==1 (a truncated final TLV, constructible because the 8-byte-aligned header extent vs attacker-chosen optlen advances lets the cursor land on a lone final byte), nh[off+1] reads one byte past the option area that the callers pskb_may_pull'ed (they pull only skb_transport_offset + ((hdrlen+1)<<3), so the final TLV ends exactly at the pulled boundary). PADN body reads nh[off+i] likewise lack a per-option clamp. Identical to the seed mptcp_get_options missing 'if (length < 2) return' between kind byte and size byte; same code shape was reported low-confidence on s01 (fact f002).

FINDING 2 (low confidence): s02:net/bridge/br_netfilter_ipv6.c:60-67, quote 'while (len > 0) {
		int optlen = nh[off + 1] + 2;

		switch (nh[off]) {
		case IPV6_TLV_PAD1:
			optlen = 1;
			break;'. br_nf_check_hbh_len() (line 46, called from br_validate_ipv6 line 132 on every bridged IPv6 packet with bridge-nf active) has the identical shape: the initializer dereferences nh[off+1] before the type switch; PAD1 merely overwrites optlen afterwards; the sole bound 'if ((raw + len) - skb->data > skb_headlen(skb)) goto bad' covers the whole-header extent only, not the 2 bytes needed by the final TLV; the JUMBO case re-derefs nh[off+1] at line 72. One-byte over-read past the HBH option area plus unvalidated 'off += optlen; len -= optlen' advance.

SAFE (validated-equals-used guards present, exact fixed shape): net/sched/act_csum.c:456 ('while (len > 1)'), net/ipv4/ip_options.c:274 ('if (unlikely(l < 2))' before optptr[1], optlen<=l clamp), net/ipv6/calipso.c:808 (offset+1>=opt_len before tlv[offset+1]), net/ipv6/ah6.c:123/167 ('if (len < 2) goto bad' before opt[off+1], len<optlen before advance), net/ipv6/ndisc.c:232, net/ipv6/netfilter/ip6t_hbh.c:102/122 (hdrlen<1 then hdrlen<2 via skb_header_pointer), net/ipv6/netfilter/ip6t_rt.c:63, net/ipv6/seg6.c:59 (trailing<sizeof(tlv) before tlv->len), net/ipv6/seg6_local.c:155 (pskb_may_pull full hdrlen before validate), net/netfilter/nft_exthdr.c:30 (i < tcphdr_len - 1 before opt[offset+1]), net/ipv6/datagram.c:653 (trusted re-parse of input-validated headers), net/ipv6/exthdrs.c:575 (RPL SRH, n-derived pulls match allocation). net/ipv6/exthdrs_core.c:134 ipv6_find_tlv was deep-read and classified safe (pre-loop offset+2<=packet_len and header-extent bound keep the residual len==1 read inside the packet), with the PAD1-cursor caveat recorded in limitations.

LIMITATIONS: both findings are structural hypotheses - no KASAN/compile reproducer (read-only tree, no build env), and the one-byte read usually stays inside the skb head allocation, hence low confidence; not deep-read: mip6.c, exthdrs_offload.c, ip6t_srh.c, ip6_offload.c GRO walkers, xt_sctp.c, ebtables.c; only net/ of s02 was audited, drivers/ not exhaustively scanned.
